The ``ligpsport.cnx`` module is derived from the GPXtoCNXConverter
project's GPX-to-CNX serialiser. The conversion algorithm — the
second-difference ``<Tracks>`` encoding, the distance / ascent /
descent metric calculation, the ``<Route>`` XML layout including the
self-closing ``<Navs />`` quirk and the UTF-8 BOM — was reverse-
engineered there. We reimplemented it in pure stdlib (no fitparse,
no Decimal-context inheritance) and wired it into the ligpsport BLE
upload path, but the file format expertise belongs to the upstream
author.

A verbatim copy of the upstream Apache 2.0 license is preserved at
``LICENSES/GPXtoCNXConverter-LICENSE``.

The GUI ``POI Types Editor`` tool from the upstream project is not
incorporated; only the GPX→CNX conversion logic is reused.

ligpsport itself is MIT-licensed (see ``LICENSE``). The Apache 2.0
terms apply only to the derivative work in ``ligpsport/cnx.py``.
